011658022429343,0.3477025548443531,0.3511592746504942,0.3712811890789401,0.38565586858865414,0.41038582230318776,0.36309501955145335,0.337162602306484,0.35346934595626395,0.3501237778046291,0.3342006221379629,0.35969599187676493,0.3507526791983034,0.3363389111720177,0.3201149131176745,0.33297352928257806],"years":[2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024]}},"statement0":"<p style=\"margin-bottom: 12px;\">The word <span  \"><i>\"irregular\" </i></span> is mentioned two or more times in <span style=\"color: rgba(255, 89, 98, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">0.4%</span> of neuroscience papers' Results sections, as of 2020-2024. </p>Among 2020-2024 papers containing <span  \"><i>\"irregular\" </i></span>, <span style=\"color: rgba(94, 184, 242, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">32.4%</span> of reported significant p-values (p < .05) are fragile (.01 \u2264 p < .05) - i.e., barely fall under the standard significance threshold. This is a lower than the typical Psychology paper (median shown for reference); relative to other words, papers with <span  \"><i>\"irregular\" </i></span> are in the bottom <span style=\"color: rgba(3, 152, 252, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">6<sup>th</sup></span> percentile of fragile p-value percentages (lower = better). Note, strong/weak p-values highly predict replicability(see <a href=\"../assets/pdf/Bogdan_2025_PsyChange_Manuscript_SuppMat.pdf\">Supplemental Materials 7.3 of the associated paper</a>).","statement1":"As of 2020-2024, papers containing <span  \"><i>\"irregular\" </i></span> tend to be published in lower impact factor journals (<span style=\"color: rgba(105, 219, 99, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">4<sup>th</sup></span> percentile among all words)  and tend to be cited less (<span style=\"color: rgba(255, 168, 82, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">11<sup>st</sup></span> percentile word). In general, this word is negatively associated with university ranking, such that higher-ranked institutions are less likely to publish papers containing <span  \"><i>\"irregular\" </i></span> (<span style=\"color: rgba(170, 117, 250, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">2<sup>nd</sup></span> percentile). "}